From: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: use QDMA WAN channel 0 on AN7563

The AN7563 vendor active-Ethernet WAN driver uses a dedicated QDMA
instance and fixes ordinary WAN traffic to channel 0.  The queue field
is still selected independently from the packet priority.

The common driver instead derives the channel from the GDM port id.
Since the AN7563 WAN is connected to GDM2, this maps its traffic to
QDMA1 channel 2 (netdev queues 16 through 23), differing from the
channel 0 selected by the vendor ae_wan transmit path.  The same
difference is also stored in PPE flow entries for hardware-forwarded
traffic.

Select channel 0 for both AN7563 GDM2 software transmit and PPE flow
entries, matching the vendor driver.  Keep the existing channel
selection for DSA/LAN traffic and other SoCs.

Signed-off-by: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 5 ++++-
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2619,7 +2619,10 @@ static u16 airoha_dev_select_queue(struc
 	 * index, rely on port id otherwise. Select QoS queue based on the
 	 * skb priority.
 	 */
-	channel = netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) ? skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) : port->id;
+	if (dev->eth->soc->version == 0x7563 && port->id == AIROHA_GDM2_IDX)
+		channel = 0;
+	else
+		channel = netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) ? skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) : port->id;
 	channel = channel % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS;
 	queue = skb->priority % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES;
 	queue = channel * AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES + queue;

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -398,7 +398,11 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(
 			 * channel according to the DSA user port index, rely
 			 * on port id otherwise.
 			 */
-			channel = dsa_port >= 0 ? dsa_port : port->id;
+			if (eth->soc->version == 0x7563 &&
+			    port->id == AIROHA_GDM2_IDX)
+				channel = 0;
+			else
+				channel = dsa_port >= 0 ? dsa_port : port->id;
 			channel = channel % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS;
 			priority = rt_tos2priority(dsfield);
 			priority = priority % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES;
